10.6.5 Acoustic Lining of Duct
Acoustic lining of duct should be carried out as follows:
a) The inside surface of duct on which the acoustic lining is to be provided should be thoroughly cleaned with wire brush and rendered free from all dust and grease;
b) The materials to be used for duct lining should be 25 mm thick resin bonded fiberglass having density of
48 kg/m3.  Open cell flexible elastomeric foam having density of minimum 140 kg/m3 specially
formulated only for sound attenuation not for inside duct surfaces, due to its poor fire and smoke emission risks;
c) The insulation should be fixed inside the duct using suitable adhesive and covered with fibre glass tissue paper.  Open cell flexible elastomeric Foam should be installed with eco-friendly low VOC adhesive elastomeric foam should pass the tests (for test procedure special publications may be referred) for
